# WHICH INPUTS EACH PINNED THIRD-PARTY ACTION DECLARES. Held by `cargo xtask check-workflows`
# (xtask/src/workflows/with_keys.rs).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A `with:` key an action does not declare is not an error on the runner. It
# is `##[warning]Unexpected input(s) '<key>', valid inputs are [...]` and then the action's own
# DEFAULT for the input the author meant - so the step is green, the log carries the only witness,
# and the entry looks configured. `.github/actions/causality-target-cache` passed `path:` to
# `nix-community/cache-nix-action`, whose input is `paths:`, for 21 runs: the action took its
# default path list and cached a second copy of the Nix store instead of the target directory the
# key named. Nothing in this repository read that warning, and nothing could.
#
# WHY A RECORD RATHER THAN A LOOKUP. The gate runs inside a nix derivation with no network, so it
# cannot fetch an action's manifest. It also does not need to: an input list is a property of a
# COMMIT, and every `uses:` here is pinned to a full sha. So an entry cannot rot while its pin
# holds - and when a pin moves, the sha below stops matching and the gate fails closed until
# somebody re-reads the new manifest. That refresh is the review moment this record buys.
#
# HOW TO REFRESH ONE ENTRY. Read the top-level `inputs:` keys of `action.yml` (or `action.yaml`) at
# the new sha - `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/<sha>/action.yml` answers 200 for
# a public action with no credential - and replace that block. Nothing is derived: the names below
# are the manifest's own keys, in the manifest's own order.
#
# READ ON 2026-09-10, each from the sha it is filed under.
#
# WHAT THIS RECORD CANNOT SAY, next to the claim:
#
#   * NOT that a value is right. `paths: target/causality-target` and `paths: /dev/null` are the
#     same shape to this record. It holds the KEY set and nothing about meaning.
#   * NOT that a required input is present. An action declares `required:` per input and this
#     record drops that column deliberately: the runner enforces it, loudly, on the run.
#   * NOT the local composite actions under `.github/actions`. Their inputs are declared in this
#     repository, so a wrong key there is a diff a reviewer sees and `actionlint` already
#     validates them from the tree. The gap this closes is the actions whose manifest is NOT here.
#   * NOT reusable workflows (`<owner>/<repo>/.github/workflows/<file>@<ref>`). Those take `with:`
#     against a `workflow_call` input block, a different oracle, and this repository calls none.
#   * NOT whether `actionlint` would have caught it. It ships a metadata set for the popular
#     actions and validates local ones; it knew nothing about the action that shipped the defect,
#     which is the whole reason this record is committed rather than assumed.
#
# FORMAT: a line at column zero is `<owner>/<repo>@<sha>`; the indented lines under it are that
# sha's declared input names. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.

